window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Will contempt break Xane, or will she rise above it?</b></p> <p>In the seventh volume of the Xane series, author Mark White takes listeners on an emotional journey through the life of Xane, a character grappling with the intense emotion of contempt. As Xane navigates the pressures of fame, the invasion of privacy, and the constant scrutiny from the media and fans, she finds herself struggling to maintain her sense of self.<br> <br> Xane's journey is marked by her interactions with her bandmates—Leila, Ruby, Zoe, and Lena—as they face the challenges of being in the spotlight. The story delves into themes of setting boundaries, managing emotions, and the importance of empathy and understanding. Throughout the book, Xane engages in deep conversations with an entity known as the Analyst, who helps her understand the roots of her contempt and guides her toward emotional growth.<br> <br> As Xane learns to let go of her contempt and embrace vulnerability, she discovers the power of connection and the joy of being true to herself. <i>Contempt</i> Xane, Volume 7, is a powerful exploration of emotional intelligence, highlighting the complexities of human emotions and the journey toward self-acceptance.<br> <br> Join Xane as she rises above the storms of judgment and finds strength in her journey. This volume is a must-listen for fans of the series and anyone interested in the intricate dance of emotions.</p>"; 
